      "writtenOn": "2017-12-24T12:57:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The schema here only allow one Property, any reason why role \"id\" and \"name\" cannot be presented together?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_4daaa1d2",
        "filename": "keystone/oauth1/schema.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 15054
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-25T01:30:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "a valid input is like:\n\n{\n   \"roles\": [\n        {\"id\": xxx},\n        {\"name\": admin}\n   ] \n}\n\nyou mean it could be like this?\n\n{\n   \"roles\": [\n        {\"id\": admin\u0027s id,\n         \"name\": admin}\n   ] \n}\n\nI think it\u0027s a little redundant.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_4ccb8771",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_2d95dd40",
        "filename": "keystone/oauth1/schema.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 13063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-25T01:52:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, it\u0027s redundant here, but if user gives \"id\" as well as \"name\", should it be an exception? we can see many examples in this project.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_4daaa1d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_cdca3119",
        "filename": "keystone/oauth1/schema.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 15054
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-25T02:45:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can find other two APIs whose input can contain id and name:\n\n1. issue a token with password:\nin this API, user\u0027s, project\u0027s domain\u0027s id and name can be put together, but Keystone doesn\u0027t raise error, it just use name and ignore id. https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/auth/plugins/core.py#L150-L179\n\n2. create trust with role id and name, it\u0027s rejected by schema:\nhttps://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/trust/schema.py#L16-L28\n\nNow if we raise an other error here if id and name are specified together, it\u0027ll be an other new behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_2d95dd40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_b1d61527",
        "filename": "keystone/oauth1/schema.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-26T19:21:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t really think it makes sense to allow both id and name, I don\u0027t know why someone would want to use that. Currently the trust schema only allows one property for role so I think following that makes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_cdca3119",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_74771404",
        "filename": "keystone/oauth1/schema.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 13063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-27T10:43:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree, redundant and not make sense, but it\u0027s possible. It depends on how we see the severity of the behavior, raise exception here means user\u0027s request will be rejected even both role id and name are correct.\n\nEnd user won\u0027t know the hard requirement for the schema here unless this is documented anywhere or overwrite \"SchemaValidationError\" in order to let us know what exactly wrong in the body.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_b1d61527",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_8c874f10",
        "filename": "keystone/tests/unit/test_validation.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2403,
      "author": {
        "id": 13063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-24T12:57:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Properly, provide two properties together is not necessary but should be an exception except the case \"id\" and \"name\" are not consistent with each other.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2401,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2403,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_add24d5b",
        "filename": "keystone/tests/unit/test_validation.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2403,
      "author": {
        "id": 15054
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-25T01:30:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could do this if we support id and name together here. But I can\u0027t see some case for it. Is there any usage. IMHO, either id or name is enough.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_8c874f10",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2401,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2403,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_51b6a9fc",
        "filename": "keystone/tests/unit/test_validation.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2403,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-26T19:21:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Validating that would require two lookups, one to get by ID and one to find by name, in order to compare. I think that adds unnecessary complexity when it could be just validated at the schema layer by rejecting multiple properties.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_8c874f10",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2401,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2403,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "c0124a9299ab079b3541dd7aef9f7a7f3a87f446",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8cb3f7_d4f5c084",
        "filename": "keystone/tests/unit/test_validation.py",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2403,
      "author": {
        "id": 13063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-27T10:43:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, that kind of comparison is somehow complex, but even ignore either of them is better than raise an exception IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "bf8cb3f7_51b6a9fc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2401,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2403,
        "endChar": 46
